{"ts":"2026-07-15T17:53:49.678Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"control-snapshot-heartbeat-lease-freshness","consecutive":3,"metric":"priority"}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"control-snapshot-heartbeat-lease-freshness","metric":"priority"}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"ControlPlaneSnapshotOwner uses owner-authored ready-lease bounds, not heartbeat-cadence age, for cache freshness: staggered active-node heartbeats within unexpired leases yield fresh snapshots, while expired or missing lease evidence remains stale and schedules bounded repair. Red-on-revert producer-owner-consumer tests and one production MovieLens run prove preload admission observes the fresh outcome without accepting stale or blind snapshots.","class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."}],"frontierIds":["control-snapshot-heartbeat-lease-freshness-main"]}}
{"ts":"2026-07-15T17:55:52.700Z","type":"finding","frontier":"control-snapshot-heartbeat-lease-freshness-main","claim":"At main c02885ca the five-node MovieLens run reached the production snapshot lane 52 times over about 180 seconds but never reached the load lane: every observation was stale_usable/cache_stale_watermark. The 5s admin max-heartbeat threshold equals the heartbeat tick, while owner rows intentionally coalesce writes around 10s and carry 15s ready leases; final-poll CDC ages were 2.3-12.6s. This reproduces a permanent false-stale owner outcome rather than genuine load pressure.","kind":"repro-on-head","evidence":"test-output/reports/movielens-lagrange-service-affinity-live-2026-07-15T17-46-37-270Z.report.json","rulesOut":null,"verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
{"ts":"2026-07-15T17:55:52.738Z","type":"finding","frontier":"control-snapshot-heartbeat-lease-freshness-main","claim":"Architectural owner trace: HeartbeatService produces last_heartbeat plus ready_lease_expires_at; ControlPlaneSnapshotOwner owns freshness/repair vocabulary; MovieLens and other consumers must consume that outcome. A local 5s max-age heuristic ignores the producer's lease handoff and violates bounded stale-heartbeat tolerance. The fix boundary is the snapshot repair evaluation, preserving consumer fail-closed behavior rather than adding a demo exception or timeout.","kind":null,"evidence":"architecture/readiness-and-owner-contracts.md","rulesOut":null,"verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
